{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>אהי</b> — Some say: inverted, like איה. The correct interpretation: as if saying: אהי, where is your king?" "<b>יושיעך</b> — From [the hand of] enemies and from [the hand of] wild beasts." "<b>ושופטיך</b> — The meaning is doubled."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra reads אהי as an interrogative meaning 'where'; the final phrase rendered hyper-literally; he paraphrases the sense as 'where (איפוא) is your king.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:10.410778777Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}